{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויסעו מפני החירות", :translit "vayis'u mipnei ha'chirot", :gloss "and they journeyed from before Pi HaChirot"} {:he "מפי החירות", :translit "mipi ha'chirot", :gloss "from the mouth of Pi HaChirot"} {:he "ויסעו ביד רמה", :translit "vayis'u beyad ramah", :gloss "and they journeyed with a high hand"} {:he "שיהיו בני חורין", :translit "sheyihyu bnei chorin", :gloss "that they would be free men"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The prefix מן in מפני is read as if it bore the sense of ״high hand,״ since the journey was an act of open defiance and liberation."}], :frame {:text "The phrase ביד רמה describes Israel's departure from Egypt as an act of open, unafraid defiance (Exodus 14:8). Freedom from Egyptian bondage was the divine assurance given to Abraham at Genesis 15:13–14, where God foretells the exile and then the liberation with great possessions. The midrashic tradition reads place-names in the wilderness itinerary as encoding stages of that liberation, so that the journey מפני החירות signals the transition into open freedom, consistent with the promise of redemption.", :sources ["Exodus 14:8" "Genesis 15:13–14" "Bereshit Rabbah 48:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The prefix מן in מפני is read as if it bore the sense of ״high hand,״ since the journey was an act of open defiance and liberation.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:40.051370144Z", :model "glm-5.2"}